      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "THE AIM",
          "content": "Of the study was to establish the most frequent clinical symptoms of gastroesophageal reflux (GER) disease in children."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIAL AND METHODS",
          "content": "214 children aged from 4 months to 15 years with symptoms suggested GER. The medical documentation of children was analyzed with regard to results of clinical symptoms and 24-hour pH-monitoring."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The most frequent symptom in newborn was spitting, in children aged 1-3 was vomiting, in children aged 4-15 was stomach pain. Amongst children to 3 years recurrent bronchitis was frequent co-existent disease, in older children duodenitis or/and gastritis. Based on positive result of 24-hour pH-monitoring gastroesophageal disease was diagnosed in 184 (86%) patients. Preliminary diagnosis of GER based on the medical interview with high percentage of positive results of 24-hour pH-monitoring. The introduced results prove the medical interview to be still significant part of GER diagnosis."
        }
      ]},
